==============================================================================
0. Data and published figures
==============================================================================
Pilot (Albert 2021): TP=43 FN=11 FP=0 TN=358 n=412; Se=0.7963 Sp=1.0000 prev=0.1311
Validation (Bulilete 2021): TP=100 FN=40 FP=2 TN=1220 n=1362; Se=0.7143 Sp=0.9984 prev=0.1028
Published: frequentist N = 927 (Bulilete Methods); enrolled 1369; analysed 1362

==============================================================================
1. Initial prior and its compatibility with the pilot
==============================================================================
Base case: flat Beta(1,1) for Se, Sp and prevalence. The compatibility
check is OMITTED for a flat prior: with Beta(1,1) the predictive is uniform
and the smallest attainable tail is 1/(n+1), so it cannot flag anything
informative. The function is called once below only to show
its warning.
WARNING [flat initial prior]: flat Beta(1, 1) prior in: sensitivity (true positives) [analysis]; specificity (true negatives) [analysis]. The predictive is uniform and the smallest possible tail is 1/(n + 1); the check is not informative with a flat prior and only extreme results can be flagged.

Secondary illustration: initial prior centred on the manufacturer claim
(Se 0.933, Sp 0.994; Bulilete Background), ILLUSTRATIVE effective size
