==============================================================================
8. Interpretation
==============================================================================
1. The principal flow recommends N = 497 total participants (A = 0.8007; A(496) = 0.7985).
   The published frequentist plan was 927 and 1369 were enrolled (1362 analysed).
   The recommended N is 54% of the published plan.
2. Analysis prior: with use_in 'both' N = 258 (Sp updated prior Beta(180, 1) already
   meets the Sp width before any data are observed, see the warning in section 3),
   so the Sp criterion stops constraining N and success is driven by the prior.
   'design' is therefore the principal choice: the analysis does not borrow the pilot.
3. Two-sided full widths 0.20/0.10 give N = 612; marginal Se only gives N = 497 (one-sided).
   Se drives N in every scenario: Sp is close to 1 in the pilot (FP = 0).
4. a0 (use_in design): a0=0.25 -> N=520; a0=0.5 -> N=497; a0=1 -> N=480
   Se semi-width: 0.05 -> 1870; 0.075 -> 859; 0.125 -> 325; 0.15 -> 231
   prevalence prior: prev_init15_n20_updated -> 502; prev_init15_n100_updated -> 478; prev_replaced_15_n100 -> 467; prev_replaced_10_n100_hindsight -> 742; prev_replaced_05_n100 -> 1722
   assurance target: 0.7 -> 457; 0.9 -> 558
5. Hellinger contour (epsilon 0.01), n* range per perturbed initial prior: se: 490-505; sp: 497-497; prev: 490-502
6. Frequentist (Buderer, fixed values): principal N = 336 (Se 0.796, Sp 0.989, prev 0.131); it ignores
   prior uncertainty and the probability of reaching the width, so it is not comparable to an assured N.
   Reproduction of the published 927 from the Methods inputs: 927.
7. Post-study check: see section 6 and the CSV; interpret against the ANALYSIS prior (inferential
   reference) and the DESIGN prior (calibration). It does not choose a0.

